* VIEW-1108 SCENES: each scene number and the scenario it runs on.
*
* tools/gen_data.py writes these into build/scenes.json, the list the Makefile
* (make check) and the selftest (tools/selftest.mjs) read.  The kernel keeps its
* own copy, DATA ISNSC in VINIT (src/vdrive.f); gen_data.py stops if the two
* differ.  Scenes become situations (SITUATION cards in the scenario decks) in
* #17, which retires this file and ISNSC.  The map is ours (CLAUDE.md, Scenes):
* 1-8 run on Apollo 11 as flown, 9 on Apollo 8 as flown.
*
* Card: SCENE ID= (1..N)  SCENARIO= (a scenario's SCENARIO ID=)
*
* Earthrise
SCENE ID=1 SCENARIO=1
* Transearth coast / Earth approach
SCENE ID=2 SCENARIO=1
* Earth limb
SCENE ID=3 SCENARIO=1
* LM rendezvous
SCENE ID=4 SCENARIO=1
* LM descent
SCENE ID=5 SCENARIO=1
* Moon view
SCENE ID=6 SCENARIO=1
* Transposition and docking
SCENE ID=7 SCENARIO=1
* Docked stack in translunar coast
SCENE ID=8 SCENARIO=1
* Apollo 8 Earthrise
SCENE ID=9 SCENARIO=2
